    "turn_idx": 30,
    "turn_text": "So I was a bio major in college. I thought I was going to be a veterinarian originally, which is why I went into biology. And I ended up very interested in research and did immunology research after I graduated from school. And ended up in Seattle working at a biotech company, an early biotech company there called Zlamogenetics doing research, chimeric antibody research, for those of you who want to look that up. I was very interested in that and went back to school to business school to get my MBA. Thinking I was going to go back into biotech. I was interested in the business side of it as well. And Microsoft was recruiting folks for summer internships and I thought that would be a great thing to try for a summer and learn a lot about software, which is this interesting thing. Microsoft was still pretty small then. This was 1989. So I worked there over the summer and ended up staying and working there and ended up working for Microsoft full time after I graduated. So it wasn't necessarily a shift I",
