    "turn_text": "It doesn't just have to be software development. Go to a shop in a school. We have a lot of advanced manufacturing in my district. Have people get experience in shop, et cetera. 3D printing has been interesting and to see how kids are interacting there, both young women and men, and has changed some of those barriers and some of those stereotypes. So I do think that you're going to see a change over time because schools, it's not just about schools alone accepting people. It's about people being excited and wanting to go into those areas. I think that's the biggest change. And I think you were seeing some of that happen now. But it's going to go through to get kind of all the way through from beginning through the cycle. It's going to take a while to make sure we continue to build those numbers. And I think we're on a good path, but we've got to continue to support that.",
