  {
    "episode_id": 96371,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/6/96371.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 130,
    "turn_text": "It's a be engaged in policy, understand that policy can impact what's happening, especially in, depending on the business area you're in, you may be surprised to find out that there are policies that impact what you're doing. When we were starting a drug store, we thought we're a retail store. People come online, we're just like a drug store down the street. except in pharmacy environment, when people sent prescription drugs to the mail, it was considered mail service pharmacy. And that's a different type of pharmacy and is a different environment than a traditional retail pharmacy. And we were stuck in between. We thought we were retail, but because we shipped prescriptions through the mail, we were from a kind of more of a regulatory standpoint, thought it was a mail service pharmacy. And that's something we learned while we were going impacted, whether we could get reimbursed for insurance was definitely a hard thing. All of the businesses that you engage with involvement may have impacts that policy may have an impact, not something necessarily just broad like tax policy, but something maybe specific to the vertical you're working in. And it's incredibly important to understand that and to be engaged and involved because you can help drive policy if you're engaged and involved and have a voice so that policy actually helps your business, helps the entrepreneurial environment out there as opposed to stymies it. And the only way we get there is if folks work together and are engaged and involved.",
